# Unit 02 单词



## ancestor
- **音标**: /ˈænsestər/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 祖先；祖宗
- **例句**: Our ancestors lived in caves thousands of years ago.
- **近义词**: forefather, predecessor, progenitor
- **派生词**: ancestral (adj.), ancestry (n.)

## annual
- **音标**: /ˈænjuəl/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 年度的；每年的；年刊
- **例句**: The company holds an annual meeting every December.
- **近义词**: yearly, per annum
- **派生词**: annually (adv.)

## anticipate
- **音标**: /ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 预期；期望；预料
- **例句**: We anticipate that the project will be completed on time.
- **近义词**: expect, foresee, predict
- **派生词**: anticipation (n.), anticipated (adj.)

## apparent
- **音标**: /əˈpærənt/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 明显的；表面上的
- **例句**: It was apparent that he was lying.
- **近义词**: obvious, evident, clear
- **派生词**: apparently (adv.)

## appeal
- **音标**: /əˈpiːl/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 呼吁；吸引；上诉
- **例句**: The idea of working abroad appeals to many young people.
- **近义词**: plea, request, attract
- **派生词**: appealing (adj.)

## applaud
- **音标**: /əˈplɔːd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 鼓掌；称赞；赞同
- **例句**: The audience applauded the performance enthusiastically.
- **近义词**: clap, praise, commend
- **派生词**: applause (n.)

## apply
- **音标**: /əˈplaɪ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 申请；应用；适用
- **例句**: She applied for a job at the multinational company.
- **近义词**: request, use, implement
- **派生词**: application (n.), applicant (n.), applicable (adj.)

## appoint
- **音标**: /əˈpɔɪnt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 任命；指定；约定
- **例句**: He was appointed as the new director of the company.
- **近义词**: designate, assign, nominate
- **派生词**: appointment (n.), appointed (adj.)

## appreciate
- **音标**: /əˈpriːʃieɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 感激；欣赏；理解；增值
- **例句**: I really appreciate your help with this project.
- **近义词**: value, cherish, recognize
- **派生词**: appreciation (n.), appreciative (adj.)

## approach
- **音标**: /əˈproʊtʃ/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 接近；方法；途径
- **例句**: We need a new approach to solve this problem.
- **近义词**: method, way, access
- **派生词**: approachable (adj.)

## appropriate
- **音标**: /əˈproʊpriət/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 适当的；合适的
- **例句**: Please wear appropriate clothing for the interview.
- **近义词**: suitable, proper, fitting
- **派生词**: appropriately (adv.), inappropriate (adj.)

## approve
- **音标**: /əˈpruːv/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 批准；赞成；认可
- **例句**: The committee approved the new budget plan.
- **近义词**: authorize, endorse, sanction
- **派生词**: approval (n.), disapprove (v.)

## arise
- **音标**: /əˈraɪz/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 出现；产生；起身
- **例句**: Many problems arose during the implementation of the plan.
- **近义词**: emerge, occur, appear
- **派生词**: arising (adj.)

## arouse
- **音标**: /əˈraʊz/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 唤起；激起；引起
- **例句**: The speech aroused strong emotions among the audience.
- **近义词**: stimulate, provoke, awaken
- **派生词**: arousal (n.)

## arrange
- **音标**: /əˈreɪndʒ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 安排；整理；排列
- **例句**: She arranged the flowers in a beautiful vase.
- **近义词**: organize, plan, prepare
- **派生词**: arrangement (n.)

## arrest
- **音标**: /əˈrest/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 逮捕；阻止；吸引
- **例句**: The police arrested the suspect last night.
- **近义词**: apprehend, detain, seize
- **派生词**: arrestable (adj.)

## artificial
- **音标**: /ˌɑːrtɪˈfɪʃl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 人工的；人造的；虚假的
- **例句**: Artificial intelligence is transforming many industries.
- **近义词**: synthetic, fake, manufactured
- **派生词**: artificially (adv.)

## aspect
- **音标**: /ˈæspekt/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 方面；外观；朝向
- **例句**: We need to consider every aspect of the problem.
- **近义词**: facet, dimension, feature

## assault
- **音标**: /əˈsɔːlt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 攻击；袭击
- **例句**: The soldiers assaulted the enemy position at dawn.
- **近义词**: attack, raid, onslaught
- **派生词**: assaulter (n.)

## assemble
- **音标**: /əˈsembl/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 集合；组装；装配
- **例句**: The workers assembled the parts in the factory.
- **近义词**: gather, collect, put together
- **派生词**: assembly (n.)

## assert
- **音标**: /əˈsɜːrt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 断言；声称；维护
- **例句**: She asserted her innocence throughout the trial.
- **近义词**: declare, claim, maintain
- **派生词**: assertion (n.), assertive (adj.), assertiveness (n.)

## assess
- **音标**: /əˈses/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 评估；评价；评定
- **例句**: The teacher assessed the students' performance.
- **近义词**: evaluate, appraise, judge
- **派生词**: assessment (n.), assessor (n.)

## assign
- **音标**: /əˈsaɪn/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 分配；指派；指定
- **例句**: The teacher assigned homework to the students.
- **近义词**: allocate, designate, appoint
- **派生词**: assignment (n.)

## assist
- **音标**: /əˈsɪst/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 帮助；协助
- **例句**: The nurse assisted the doctor during the operation.
- **近义词**: help, aid, support
- **派生词**: assistance (n.), assistant (n.)

## associate
- **音标**: /əˈsoʊʃieɪt/
- **词性**: v. n. adj.
- **释义**: 联系；联想；同事
- **例句**: People often associate the color red with passion.
- **近义词**: connect, link, relate
- **派生词**: association (n.)

## assume
- **音标**: /əˈsuːm/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 假定；承担；呈现
- **例句**: We assume that the meeting will be held as scheduled.
- **近义词**: presume, suppose, undertake
- **派生词**: assumption (n.), assumed (adj.)

## assure
- **音标**: /əˈʃʊr/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 保证；使确信
- **例句**: I assure you that the product is safe to use.
- **近义词**: guarantee, promise, ensure
- **派生词**: assurance (n.), assured (adj.)

## attach
- **音标**: /əˈtætʃ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 附上；系上；使依恋
- **例句**: Please attach your resume to the email.
- **近义词**: fasten, connect, affix
- **派生词**: attachment (n.), attached (adj.)

## attain
- **音标**: /əˈteɪn/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 达到；获得；实现
- **例句**: She attained the highest score in the exam.
- **近义词**: achieve, reach, accomplish
- **派生词**: attainable (adj.), attainment (n.)

## attempt
- **音标**: /əˈtempt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 尝试；企图
- **例句**: He attempted to climb the mountain but failed.
- **近义词**: try, endeavor, strive
- **派生词**: attempted (adj.)

## attend
- **音标**: /əˈtend/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 出席；参加；照料
- **例句**: Over 200 people attended the conference.
- **近义词**: be present, go to, participate
- **派生词**: attendance (n.), attendant (n. adj.), attention (n.)

## attribute
- **音标**: /əˈtrɪbjuːt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 归因于；属性；特质
- **例句**: She attributed her success to hard work and determination.
- **近义词**: ascribe, credit, assign
- **派生词**: attribution (n.), attributable (adj.)

## audit
- **音标**: /ˈɔːdɪt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 审计；旁听
- **例句**: The company's accounts are audited every year.
- **近义词**: inspect, examine, review
- **派生词**: auditor (n.), auditing (n.)

## authority
- **音标**: /əˈθɔːrəti/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 权威；当局；权力
- **例句**: The local authority is responsible for public services.
- **近义词**: power, control, jurisdiction
- **派生词**: authoritative (adj.), authorize (v.), authorization (n.)

## automatic
- **音标**: /ˌɔːtəˈmætɪk/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 自动的；无意识的
- **例句**: The door has an automatic locking system.
- **近义词**: self-operating, mechanical, involuntary
- **派生词**: automatically (adv.), automation (n.), automate (v.)

## available
- **音标**: /əˈveɪləbl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 可用的；有空的；可获得的
- **例句**: The book is available in all major bookstores.
- **近义词**: accessible, obtainable, free
- **派生词**: availability (n.), unavailable (adj.)

## avoid
- **音标**: /əˈvɔɪd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 避免；避开；回避
- **例句**: You should avoid eating too much sugar.
- **近义词**: evade, dodge, prevent
- **派生词**: avoidance (n.), avoidable (adj.), unavoidable (adj.)

## aware
- **音标**: /əˈwer/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 意识到的；知道的
- **例句**: Are you aware of the risks involved?
- **近义词**: conscious, informed, alert
- **派生词**: awareness (n.), unaware (adj.)

## awful
- **音标**: /ˈɔːfl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 可怕的；糟糕的；极大的
- **例句**: The weather was awful during our vacation.
- **近义词**: terrible, dreadful, horrible
- **派生词**: awfully (adv.)

## awkward
- **音标**: /ˈɔːkwərd/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 尴尬的；笨拙的；不合适的
- **例句**: There was an awkward silence after his comment.
- **近义词**: clumsy, uncomfortable, embarrassing
- **派生词**: awkwardly (adv.), awkwardness (n.)
